---
description: One builder writes each change
alwaysApply: true
---

One change has one builder, named on the Linear ticket. Claude Code on Opus 5.5 writes this app's features and fixes. The Cursor chat, on Grok 4.7, reviews a risky diff without editing it, and updates status and leftover docs after that pull request merges. Do not implement a ticket whose builder is Claude Code. A ticket where Claude Code has commented that it started is Claude Code's. A cloud agent is the builder only when the ticket says so, and uses the branch name Linear copies for that ticket: branch from origin/main, use Grok or Composer, open a draft pull request, do not merge, and do not write "My read". Leave files another open pull request is already editing. The full rule is docs/workflow.md, section "Which tool writes the code".
